infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Microbenchmark prediction vs production verdict
  desc Same change, two measurements — only the production diff decides whether it ships
  compares
    - label Microbenchmark — prediction
      children
        - label 5× faster in isolation
          desc The new algorithm benchmarked alone, with no system load around it
        - label Hot function 15% → 8% CPU
          desc The local frame genuinely shrank — a real, measurable local win
        - label Reads as a clear improvement
          desc Ship it — but only if you stop measuring at the function boundary
    - label Production profile — verdict
      children
        - label Total CPU% unchanged
          desc The 7 saved points reappeared elsewhere — no system-wide gain
        - label p99 latency got worse
          desc The headline SLO metric regressed, not improved
        - label New GC hotspot emerged
          desc Extra allocations raised GC pressure and slowed other paths
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e
